# Operational config -- NO SECRETS. Copy to onboarding/.env.config and edit
# freely. onboarding/.env.config is gitignored (machine-specific choices),
# but unlike onboarding/.env it holds nothing that authenticates anything,
# so it is safe for anyone -- and any agent -- to open and edit directly.

# --- Public base URL ---
# Required -- this service refuses to start without it (onboarding/main.py's
# lifespan). Needs to be this service's own real public URL: every frame
# that drives a full-page redirect to an external site (GitHub's App
# Manifest flow, Supabase's OAuth authorize screen) builds its
# redirect_url/callback URL from this value, so a wrong or missing value
# breaks those flows -- in GitHub's case, only after the visitor has already
# created a real App whose one-time credentials are then unrecoverable (see
# onboarding/config.py's own validator comment). Auto-populated on Render as
# RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL, same as app/'s own PUBLIC_BASE_URL; set locally for
# local development.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
